thcare  workers  and other trusted leaders in our  communities  we have a lot of uh faith that our seal  initiative  will make a difference in the states  that we have launched it  and we continue to work on expanding it  um  and turn towards vaccine uptake  so really creating the structures to  promote  make it easy for people to get  vaccinated such as  an event like this and other houses of  worship opening up  to um to being vaccinated  now i want to just close by saying that  i'm confident that this effort is going  to make a difference  i think all of us are eager uh to be  able to again see our loved ones  and share with people in person not zoom  i was vaccinated myself a little over  two weeks ago got my second shot  i went through the dc vaccine website it  wasn't easy but i got it done  and i think the easier we can make it as  we get more and more  people vaccinated the better we'll be  thanks everyone for um being here  for organizing this uh it really is  important  for all of us to be together to work  towards a better future  thank you  [Music]  i'm marianne buddy bishop of the  episcopal diocese of washington  after hearing such important remarks  from  our scientific and medical and  governmental communities  and in the presence of such esteemed  colleagues  in faith i'm honored to close this  portion  of our gathering in prayer may we begin  by simply calling to mind all those  we've lost  and those who suffer  and we thank you gracious god for all  who have worked so tirelessly  to bring the scourge of covet 19 in this  land and around the world  to an end we lament  the inequities and the injustices that  have caused so many to suffer needlessly  and we pray that this effort along with  others will help  overcome some of the disparities that  have divided us  let this vaccination effort be our  our marking event to create justice in  our society and our health care system  and to restore the trust that is so  needed for us to move forward  most 